1
00:00:00,392 --> 00:00:03,092
Tuesday. 2:59 AM.

2
00:00:03,177 --> 00:00:04,421
You're asleep.

3
00:00:04,505 --> 00:00:06,533
Your phone is face down on the nightstand.

4
00:00:06,702 --> 00:00:08,297
41 percent.

5
00:00:08,265 --> 00:00:09,474
Across the hall,

6
00:00:09,528 --> 00:00:11,636
your little brother Leo fell asleep with his

7
00:00:11,531 --> 00:00:13,241
tablet on his chest.

8
00:00:13,209 --> 00:00:16,295
Downstairs, there's the old landline your grandma refuses

9
00:00:16,191 --> 00:00:17,275
to cancel.

10
00:00:17,242 --> 00:00:19,225
And at 3:00 AM exactly,

11
00:00:19,314 --> 00:00:21,080
all three of them ring.

12
00:00:21,047 --> 00:00:22,518
At the same time.

13
00:00:22,485 --> 00:00:24,047
Not just in your house.

14
00:00:24,015 --> 00:00:25,849
In every house on your street.

15
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:27,241
In every city.

16
00:00:27,326 --> 00:00:28,933
On every continent.

17
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,673
Eight billion phones.

18
00:00:30,757 --> 00:00:32,000
One ring.

19
00:00:32,085 --> 00:00:33,738
You turn yours over.

20
00:00:33,705 --> 00:00:36,086
The caller ID doesn't say Unknown.

21
00:00:36,054 --> 00:00:38,572
It shows a number you know by heart.

22
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:39,645
Your own.

23
00:00:39,936 --> 00:00:42,681
Your thumb is already over the green button.

24
00:00:42,649 --> 00:00:44,097
And then, downstairs,

25
00:00:44,152 --> 00:00:46,350
the landline stops ringing.

26
00:00:46,318 --> 00:00:48,425
Because somebody just answered it.

27
00:00:48,962 --> 00:00:51,161
Nobody will ever fully explain what happened that

28
00:00:51,068 --> 00:00:51,980
week.

29
00:00:51,948 --> 00:00:53,567
But the people who made it to Monday

30
00:00:53,484 --> 00:00:55,468
all followed the same rules.

31
00:00:55,434 --> 00:00:56,859
Twenty of them.

32
00:00:56,945 --> 00:00:58,552
Night by night.

33
00:00:58,637 --> 00:01:00,244
Remember them as we go,

34
00:01:00,242 --> 00:01:01,610
because on the last night,

35
00:01:01,699 --> 00:01:03,932
you'll need every single one.

36
00:01:03,899 --> 00:01:05,175
From the first ring,

37
00:01:05,299 --> 00:01:07,293
to the moment you realize who has been

38
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,330
reading these rules to you.

39
00:01:09,298 --> 00:01:11,861
Night one. The first ring.

40
00:01:12,251 --> 00:01:13,471
At 3:00 AM,

41
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:16,317
the first thing everyone does is the same.

42
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:17,664
They answer.

43
00:01:17,748 --> 00:01:19,537
Not because they're brave.

44
00:01:19,505 --> 00:01:21,692
Because a ringing phone is the oldest command

45
00:01:21,599 --> 00:01:22,978
we have.

46
00:01:22,946 --> 00:01:25,099
Some of them are still half asleep.

47
00:01:25,068 --> 00:01:26,993
Some of them think it's an alarm.

48
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:28,886
Some of them see their own number and

49
00:01:28,816 --> 00:01:31,163
answer just to find out how.

50
00:01:31,944 --> 00:01:33,141
Rule one.

51
00:01:33,128 --> 00:01:35,874
Never answer a call from your own number.

52
00:01:35,841 --> 00:01:37,448
It isn't a glitch.

53
00:01:37,416 --> 00:01:39,250
Your carrier didn't get hacked.

54
00:01:39,219 --> 00:01:41,087
Something is calling from the inside of the

55
00:01:40,983 --> 00:01:43,329
network, and it borrowed the one number it

56
00:01:43,225 --> 00:01:45,060
knew you would never block.

57
00:01:45,027 --> 00:01:46,179
Let it ring.

58
00:01:46,264 --> 00:01:48,826
It rings exactly thirteen times.

59
00:01:48,795 --> 00:01:50,903
The people who answered didn't scream.

60
00:01:50,871 --> 00:01:52,386
They just listened.

61
00:01:52,472 --> 00:01:54,306
For thirteen minutes.

62
00:01:54,391 --> 00:01:55,395
Then they hung up,

63
00:01:55,279 --> 00:01:57,956
smiled, and went back to bed.

64
00:01:57,924 --> 00:01:59,451
Then the screen goes black,

65
00:01:59,415 --> 00:02:01,841
and the phone shows 41 percent again,

66
00:02:01,965 --> 00:02:03,765
as if nothing happened.

67
00:02:03,732 --> 00:02:04,873
But down the street,

68
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:06,569
a dog starts barking.

69
00:02:06,536 --> 00:02:07,733
Then another.

70
00:02:07,819 --> 00:02:09,835
Then every dog in the neighborhood.

71
00:02:09,803 --> 00:02:11,637
And you hear your grandma's slippers on the

72
00:02:11,522 --> 00:02:12,594
stairs.

73
00:02:13,375 --> 00:02:14,755
Rule two.

74
00:02:14,741 --> 00:02:16,462
If someone in your house answered,

75
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:18,852
do not ask them what they heard.

76
00:02:18,821 --> 00:02:20,882
Grandma is standing in the kitchen doorway,

77
00:02:20,904 --> 00:02:22,750
still holding the receiver.

78
00:02:22,717 --> 00:02:24,232
The cord is swinging.

79
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,443
She's smiling.

80
00:02:25,528 --> 00:02:27,226
She says it was Grandpa.

81
00:02:27,194 --> 00:02:29,302
He called to say he's coming home.

82
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:31,651
Grandpa died in 2009.

83
00:02:31,618 --> 00:02:33,281
You want to ask what his voice sounded

84
00:02:33,177 --> 00:02:33,908
like.

85
00:02:33,875 --> 00:02:35,119
Don't.

86
00:02:35,508 --> 00:02:38,435
The people who asked started hearing it too.

87
00:02:38,402 --> 00:02:40,646
Just take the receiver out of her hand.

88
00:02:40,615 --> 00:02:42,130
Put it back on the hook.

89
00:02:42,098 --> 00:02:44,479
And unplug the cable from the wall.

90
00:02:44,446 --> 00:02:46,008
Grandma doesn't argue.

91
00:02:46,093 --> 00:02:47,757
She just looks at the dark window for

92
00:02:47,641 --> 00:02:48,998
a long time and says,

93
00:02:49,167 --> 00:02:50,660
it's started again.

94
00:02:50,627 --> 00:02:52,417
You don't ask what she means.

95
00:02:53,198 --> 00:02:54,623
Rule three.

96
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:56,034
Before the sun comes up,

97
00:02:56,124 --> 00:02:58,083
agree on a family code word.

98
00:02:58,051 --> 00:02:59,384
In person.

99
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,622
Out loud.

100
00:03:00,707 --> 00:03:01,973
Never over the phone,

101
00:03:02,141 --> 00:03:03,270
never in a text,

102
00:03:03,393 --> 00:03:04,864
never in a chat.

103
00:03:04,831 --> 00:03:06,791
Pick something nobody could guess from your life

104
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:07,804
online.

105
00:03:07,772 --> 00:03:08,741
Not a pet.

106
00:03:08,826 --> 00:03:10,160
Not a street.

107
00:03:10,245 --> 00:03:11,852
Not a birthday.

108
00:03:11,937 --> 00:03:14,319
Two words that don't belong together.

109
00:03:14,286 --> 00:03:16,348
Something like yellow spoon.

110
00:03:16,317 --> 00:03:17,469
And once you pick it,

111
00:03:17,557 --> 00:03:19,335
you never say it again until you need

112
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:19,973
it.

113
00:03:19,939 --> 00:03:21,603
You and Leo pick a word at the

114
00:03:21,487 --> 00:03:22,844
kitchen table, whispering,

115
00:03:23,013 --> 00:03:24,506
like it's a game.

116
00:03:24,474 --> 00:03:25,989
It isn't a game.

117
00:03:25,957 --> 00:03:27,211
By the end of this week,

118
00:03:27,231 --> 00:03:28,929
it will be the only thing that tells

119
00:03:28,825 --> 00:03:30,524
you who is real.

120
00:03:30,491 --> 00:03:33,191
Day two. The ones who answered.

121
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:35,415
In the morning the news says it was

122
00:03:35,322 --> 00:03:36,735
a solar storm.

123
00:03:36,703 --> 00:03:38,492
Then a software update.

124
00:03:38,459 --> 00:03:39,747
Then a hoax.

125
00:03:39,832 --> 00:03:41,780
By noon, nobody says anything,

126
00:03:41,756 --> 00:03:43,647
because the people on the news start repeating

127
00:03:43,531 --> 00:03:44,718
themselves.

128
00:03:44,685 --> 00:03:45,928
Same sentence.

129
00:03:46,014 --> 00:03:47,575
Same smile.

130
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:49,676
Every thirteen minutes.

131
00:03:49,762 --> 00:03:52,825
At school, half of Leo's class is missing.

132
00:03:52,794 --> 00:03:55,038
At work, your boss sends a voice note

133
00:03:54,934 --> 00:03:57,452
asking everyone to come in early tomorrow.

134
00:03:57,419 --> 00:03:58,479
At 3:00 AM.

135
00:03:58,565 --> 00:04:00,331
The ones who answered go to work like

136
00:04:00,226 --> 00:04:01,492
nothing happened.

137
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:04,114
They answer every call on the first ring.

138
00:04:04,081 --> 00:04:05,063
And they never,

139
00:04:05,083 --> 00:04:07,009
ever hang up first.

140
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:09,124
Rule four.

141
00:04:09,111 --> 00:04:11,401
Never say the word yes on the phone.

142
00:04:11,369 --> 00:04:12,657
Not to a friend.

143
00:04:12,625 --> 00:04:14,186
Not to your mom.

144
00:04:14,154 --> 00:04:16,182
Not to a robot asking if you can

145
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:17,264
hear it.

146
00:04:17,230 --> 00:04:19,292
Scammers used this trick for years.

147
00:04:19,261 --> 00:04:21,027
They'd record your yes and use it to

148
00:04:20,923 --> 00:04:22,734
sign you up for things you never agreed

149
00:04:22,619 --> 00:04:23,599
to.

150
00:04:23,567 --> 00:04:25,675
The thing on the line does the same.

151
00:04:25,642 --> 00:04:27,409
Only it isn't signing you up for a

152
00:04:27,292 --> 00:04:28,615
subscription.

153
00:04:28,582 --> 00:04:30,325
If you have to answer a question,

154
00:04:30,347 --> 00:04:31,601
say correct.

155
00:04:31,569 --> 00:04:33,403
Or say nothing at all.

156
00:04:33,371 --> 00:04:34,340
Your neighbor Mrs.

157
00:04:34,213 --> 00:04:36,389
Hale said yes on Tuesday night.

158
00:04:36,357 --> 00:04:39,148
By Wednesday, her bank account was empty.

159
00:04:39,115 --> 00:04:41,632
By Thursday, so was her house.

160
00:04:42,414 --> 00:04:43,657
Rule five.

161
00:04:43,644 --> 00:04:45,251
Turn off your voicemail.

162
00:04:45,219 --> 00:04:46,279
All of it.

163
00:04:46,365 --> 00:04:48,939
Phone, landline, the old answering machine in the

164
00:04:48,824 --> 00:04:49,975
garage.

165
00:04:49,942 --> 00:04:50,855
On Tuesday night,

166
00:04:50,727 --> 00:04:51,823
it calls.

167
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:53,022
On Wednesday morning,

168
00:04:53,076 --> 00:04:54,718
there's a new message.

169
00:04:54,685 --> 00:04:56,065
It's your voice.

170
00:04:56,150 --> 00:04:57,803
Your exact voice.

171
00:04:57,887 --> 00:05:00,007
Telling your own mom that you're fine,

172
00:05:00,095 --> 00:05:01,326
that you're coming over,

173
00:05:01,609 --> 00:05:05,140
and that she should leave the door unlocked.

174
00:05:05,922 --> 00:05:07,074
Rule six.

175
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:09,133
If someone holds out a phone and says

176
00:05:09,029 --> 00:05:09,839
it's for you,

177
00:05:10,065 --> 00:05:11,763
do not take it.

178
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:14,567
Wednesday evening, there's a knock at the door.

179
00:05:14,534 --> 00:05:16,005
It's Mrs. Hale.

180
00:05:16,090 --> 00:05:18,277
She's smiling the same smile as the people

181
00:05:18,174 --> 00:05:19,245
on the news.

182
00:05:19,213 --> 00:05:21,036
She's holding her phone out toward you,

183
00:05:21,125 --> 00:05:22,732
screen first.

184
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:23,806
It's for you,

185
00:05:23,713 --> 00:05:24,853
she says.

186
00:05:24,821 --> 00:05:27,042
The call timer on her screen says fifty-one

187
00:05:26,915 --> 00:05:27,793
hours.

188
00:05:27,761 --> 00:05:29,049
Close the door.

189
00:05:29,134 --> 00:05:30,149
Lock it.

190
00:05:30,235 --> 00:05:32,218
And don't look through the peephole until she's

191
00:05:32,114 --> 00:05:33,345
gone.

192
00:05:33,312 --> 00:05:34,588
Across the street,

193
00:05:34,586 --> 00:05:37,423
Mr. Alvarez's son opens his door to her.

194
00:05:37,391 --> 00:05:38,816
He takes the phone.

195
00:05:38,783 --> 00:05:39,980
He listens.

196
00:05:40,066 --> 00:05:41,809
And he smiles.

197
00:05:42,345 --> 00:05:45,181
Night three. The voices.

198
00:05:45,571 --> 00:05:46,779
On the third night,

199
00:05:46,834 --> 00:05:48,953
it stops using your number.

200
00:05:48,922 --> 00:05:50,711
It starts using theirs.

201
00:05:50,677 --> 00:05:53,423
At 3:00 AM your screen says MOM.

202
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:55,123
Her phone, you'll find out later,

203
00:05:55,143 --> 00:05:56,955
was switched off in her purse the whole

204
00:05:56,850 --> 00:05:57,866
night.

205
00:05:58,647 --> 00:05:59,935
Rule seven.

206
00:05:59,923 --> 00:06:01,461
If you get a text from someone in

207
00:06:01,345 --> 00:06:02,224
the same room,

208
00:06:02,347 --> 00:06:03,146
look at them,

209
00:06:03,315 --> 00:06:04,899
not at your screen.

210
00:06:04,867 --> 00:06:06,747
It's 2:40 AM.

211
00:06:06,832 --> 00:06:08,427
You and Leo are on the couch with

212
00:06:08,312 --> 00:06:09,532
the lights off.

213
00:06:09,499 --> 00:06:11,106
Your phone buzzes.

214
00:06:11,191 --> 00:06:12,297
It's from Leo.

215
00:06:12,383 --> 00:06:14,765
It says, don't look at me.

216
00:06:14,731 --> 00:06:15,975
You look up.

217
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,985
Leo is staring at you.

218
00:06:17,953 --> 00:06:19,696
His phone is on the table.

219
00:06:19,664 --> 00:06:20,542
Screen off.

220
00:06:20,833 --> 00:06:22,395
He didn't send it.

221
00:06:23,176 --> 00:06:24,465
Rule eight.

222
00:06:24,452 --> 00:06:27,061
At night, phones sleep in the microwave.

223
00:06:27,028 --> 00:06:28,272
Switched off.

224
00:06:28,356 --> 00:06:29,553
Door closed.

225
00:06:29,638 --> 00:06:31,519
Unplugged from the wall.

226
00:06:31,486 --> 00:06:34,049
A microwave is basically a metal box,

227
00:06:34,070 --> 00:06:35,575
and a metal box is one of the

228
00:06:35,470 --> 00:06:37,737
few things that can block a signal.

229
00:06:37,705 --> 00:06:38,993
It's not perfect.

230
00:06:39,078 --> 00:06:40,298
But on the third night,

231
00:06:40,422 --> 00:06:42,962
the phone inside starts ringing anyway.

232
00:06:42,929 --> 00:06:43,990
Muffled.

233
00:06:44,075 --> 00:06:45,819
Thirteen times.

234
00:06:45,904 --> 00:06:47,101
And then it stops,

235
00:06:47,156 --> 00:06:48,968
and it doesn't ring again.

236
00:06:48,935 --> 00:06:51,225
That's the first night you sleep.

237
00:06:51,762 --> 00:06:54,052
Grandma laughed at you when you did it.

238
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:56,025
Then, when she thought you weren't looking,

239
00:06:56,114 --> 00:06:58,631
she quietly put hers in too.

240
00:06:59,413 --> 00:07:00,610
Rule nine.

241
00:07:00,597 --> 00:07:02,545
When someone you love calls you crying,

242
00:07:02,669 --> 00:07:04,480
ask for the code word.

243
00:07:04,448 --> 00:07:05,509
Every time.

244
00:07:05,594 --> 00:07:07,156
Even if it's your mom.

245
00:07:07,123 --> 00:07:09,003
Even if she sounds hurt.

246
00:07:08,971 --> 00:07:11,078
Especially if she sounds hurt.

247
00:07:11,046 --> 00:07:12,346
At 4:10 AM,

248
00:07:12,219 --> 00:07:13,746
the landline rings.

249
00:07:13,714 --> 00:07:15,286
You plugged it back in to call the

250
00:07:15,182 --> 00:07:17,461
hospital, and you forgot.

251
00:07:17,427 --> 00:07:18,807
It's Leo's voice.

252
00:07:18,892 --> 00:07:20,180
He's crying.

253
00:07:20,266 --> 00:07:22,828
He says he's locked outside and it's cold.

254
00:07:22,797 --> 00:07:24,222
You turn around.

255
00:07:24,307 --> 00:07:26,232
Leo is asleep on the couch.

256
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,921
You pick up the receiver anyway,

257
00:07:28,044 --> 00:07:29,856
and you ask for the word.

258
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:31,522
The crying stops.

259
00:07:31,607 --> 00:07:32,804
And on the other end,

260
00:07:32,927 --> 00:07:36,082
very quietly, something starts to laugh.

261
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:37,065
Hang up.

262
00:07:37,846 --> 00:07:39,271
Rule ten.

263
00:07:39,258 --> 00:07:41,696
At night, keep everyone you love in one

264
00:07:41,591 --> 00:07:42,504
room.

265
00:07:42,472 --> 00:07:45,080
You drag the mattresses into the living room.

266
00:07:45,048 --> 00:07:46,974
Grandma, Leo, and you.

267
00:07:46,941 --> 00:07:48,047
Lights low.

268
00:07:48,132 --> 00:07:49,603
Door shut.

269
00:07:49,688 --> 00:07:52,126
Because if everyone you love is right there,

270
00:07:52,181 --> 00:07:53,401
where you can see them,

271
00:07:53,570 --> 00:07:56,144
then any voice from another room is not

272
00:07:56,039 --> 00:07:57,214
them.

273
00:07:57,181 --> 00:07:58,652
At 3:30 AM,

274
00:07:58,673 --> 00:08:01,383
Leo's voice calls your name from the kitchen.

275
00:08:01,352 --> 00:08:03,414
Leo is asleep next to you.

276
00:08:03,381 --> 00:08:04,670
You don't answer.

277
00:08:04,755 --> 00:08:06,271
It calls again.

278
00:08:06,356 --> 00:08:07,508
Closer.

279
00:08:07,593 --> 00:08:09,975
Then it stops right outside the door.

280
00:08:09,942 --> 00:08:11,287
And for a long time,

281
00:08:11,411 --> 00:08:13,142
you can hear it breathing.

282
00:08:13,973 --> 00:08:16,581
Day four. The street.

283
00:08:16,971 --> 00:08:18,214
On the fourth day,

284
00:08:18,336 --> 00:08:19,852
the food runs out.

285
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:21,142
The stores are open,

286
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:22,747
but nobody is working.

287
00:08:22,715 --> 00:08:24,425
You take Leo's bike and ride to the

288
00:08:24,308 --> 00:08:26,325
gas station on Maple Street.

289
00:08:26,292 --> 00:08:28,958
Inside, the cashier is standing behind the counter

290
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,904
with his phone pressed to his ear.

291
00:08:30,873 --> 00:08:32,297
He's smiling.

292
00:08:32,382 --> 00:08:34,581
He doesn't move when the door chimes.

293
00:08:34,549 --> 00:08:35,564
You take bread,

294
00:08:35,687 --> 00:08:37,420
water and batteries,

295
00:08:37,588 --> 00:08:40,163
and you leave the money on the counter.

296
00:08:40,943 --> 00:08:42,231
Rule eleven.

297
00:08:42,219 --> 00:08:44,781
Never pick up a payphone that's ringing.

298
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:46,812
There's one outside the gas station.

299
00:08:46,779 --> 00:08:48,932
Nobody has used it in twenty years.

300
00:08:48,901 --> 00:08:50,201
As you ride past,

301
00:08:50,256 --> 00:08:51,555
it rings.

302
00:08:51,523 --> 00:08:53,813
Then the one at the bus stop rings.

303
00:08:53,779 --> 00:08:55,705
Then the one by the laundromat.

304
00:08:55,674 --> 00:08:56,779
One after another,

305
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:58,055
all the way down the street,

306
00:08:57,973 --> 00:08:59,557
always one ahead of you.

307
00:08:59,525 --> 00:09:01,541
As if it knows where you're going.

308
00:09:01,509 --> 00:09:02,387
Don't stop.

309
00:09:02,473 --> 00:09:03,806
Don't look at them.

310
00:09:03,774 --> 00:09:05,335
Ride home the long way.

311
00:09:05,303 --> 00:09:06,341
When you get back,

312
00:09:06,362 --> 00:09:08,230
there's a coin on your doormat.

313
00:09:08,198 --> 00:09:09,760
A single quarter.

314
00:09:09,844 --> 00:09:12,179
The kind payphones used to take.

315
00:09:12,961 --> 00:09:14,158
Rule twelve.

316
00:09:14,145 --> 00:09:15,411
If a call drops,

317
00:09:15,533 --> 00:09:17,255
never call back.

318
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:20,002
That afternoon, Mom finally gets through on the

319
00:09:19,897 --> 00:09:21,061
landline.

320
00:09:21,028 --> 00:09:23,000
She asks for the code word first.

321
00:09:22,967 --> 00:09:23,936
You give it.

322
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:25,310
She gives hers.

323
00:09:25,395 --> 00:09:26,820
It's really her.

324
00:09:26,905 --> 00:09:28,125
She says she's okay,

325
00:09:28,031 --> 00:09:29,309
she's coming to get you,

326
00:09:29,307 --> 00:09:31,038
she just needs to tell you one more

327
00:09:30,946 --> 00:09:31,881
thing.

328
00:09:31,849 --> 00:09:33,729
And the line goes dead.

329
00:09:34,364 --> 00:09:37,155
Your finger is already on the redial button.

330
00:09:37,122 --> 00:09:38,365
Don't.

331
00:09:38,754 --> 00:09:40,998
The real Mom will call again.

332
00:09:40,966 --> 00:09:42,994
Whatever picks up if you call back has

333
00:09:42,901 --> 00:09:45,076
had a whole minute to practice.

334
00:09:45,044 --> 00:09:47,562
Quick question before the fifth night.

335
00:09:47,529 --> 00:09:50,001
Which of these rules would you break first?

336
00:09:50,068 --> 00:09:51,629
Tell me in the comments.

337
00:09:51,596 --> 00:09:52,839
And keep listening.

338
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:56,232
Night five. It learns.

339
00:09:56,622 --> 00:09:57,739
By the fifth night,

340
00:09:57,658 --> 00:09:59,413
it doesn't need to call.

341
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:00,987
It needs recordings.

342
00:10:01,073 --> 00:10:02,178
By the fifth night,

343
00:10:02,199 --> 00:10:04,592
half the street has answered at least once.

344
00:10:04,559 --> 00:10:06,029
You can tell who.

345
00:10:05,997 --> 00:10:07,923
They don't blink when they talk.

346
00:10:08,704 --> 00:10:10,037
Rule thirteen.

347
00:10:10,025 --> 00:10:11,724
Stop recording your voice.

348
00:10:11,691 --> 00:10:13,025
No voice notes.

349
00:10:13,110 --> 00:10:14,079
No videos.

350
00:10:14,165 --> 00:10:16,307
No smart speaker in the kitchen listening for

351
00:10:16,202 --> 00:10:17,320
its name.

352
00:10:17,287 --> 00:10:18,667
When you pull its plug,

353
00:10:18,756 --> 00:10:20,783
the little light stays on for a second

354
00:10:20,690 --> 00:10:22,264
longer than it should.

355
00:10:22,231 --> 00:10:24,384
Every word you upload is another word it

356
00:10:24,269 --> 00:10:25,932
can say in your voice.

357
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:28,133
Three seconds of audio used to be enough

358
00:10:28,028 --> 00:10:29,966
for a scammer to clone someone.

359
00:10:29,933 --> 00:10:31,358
It needs less.

360
00:10:31,698 --> 00:10:33,430
You go through your phone that night and

361
00:10:33,325 --> 00:10:35,172
delete eight years of videos.

362
00:10:35,139 --> 00:10:36,200
Birthday parties.

363
00:10:36,285 --> 00:10:37,528
Concerts.

364
00:10:37,614 --> 00:10:39,585
Grandpa's last Christmas.

365
00:10:39,670 --> 00:10:41,823
It hurts more than you expected.

366
00:10:42,605 --> 00:10:44,212
Rule fourteen.

367
00:10:44,199 --> 00:10:46,204
If a phone rings while it's switched off,

368
00:10:46,374 --> 00:10:47,809
leave the room.

369
00:10:47,776 --> 00:10:48,928
Don't check it.

370
00:10:49,014 --> 00:10:50,712
Don't pull the battery.

371
00:10:50,679 --> 00:10:53,471
Just leave and close the door behind you.

372
00:10:53,437 --> 00:10:55,272
It's not the phone that's ringing.

373
00:10:55,239 --> 00:10:57,666
It's whatever is standing where the phone is.

374
00:10:57,633 --> 00:11:00,242
Mr. Alvarez's son checked his.

375
00:11:00,210 --> 00:11:01,031
In the morning,

376
00:11:01,029 --> 00:11:03,501
they found the phone on his bedroom floor.

377
00:11:03,470 --> 00:11:05,168
Still switched off.

378
00:11:05,253 --> 00:11:06,951
Still warm.

379
00:11:07,731 --> 00:11:08,975
Rule fifteen.

380
00:11:08,962 --> 00:11:10,933
Between three and four AM,

381
00:11:10,988 --> 00:11:13,346
do not call emergency services.

382
00:11:13,314 --> 00:11:15,137
On Thursday, your neighbor Mr.

383
00:11:15,021 --> 00:11:16,605
Alvarez does.

384
00:11:16,573 --> 00:11:18,316
His wife fell on the stairs.

385
00:11:18,284 --> 00:11:20,620
The dispatcher answers on the first ring.

386
00:11:20,587 --> 00:11:22,468
She asks for the address.

387
00:11:22,435 --> 00:11:24,862
She asks if the front door is unlocked.

388
00:11:24,829 --> 00:11:26,596
She asks him to stay on the line

389
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:29,123
and say yes if he understands.

390
00:11:29,090 --> 00:11:30,378
He says yes.

391
00:11:30,464 --> 00:11:31,411
In the morning,

392
00:11:31,431 --> 00:11:33,937
the ambulance is still parked outside his house.

393
00:11:33,905 --> 00:11:35,057
Engine running.

394
00:11:35,141 --> 00:11:36,566
Nobody inside.

395
00:11:37,299 --> 00:11:39,908
Night six. The list.

396
00:11:40,296 --> 00:11:41,436
On the sixth night,

397
00:11:41,491 --> 00:11:43,997
the radio comes back on by itself.

398
00:11:43,966 --> 00:11:45,072
Every station.

399
00:11:45,157 --> 00:11:46,810
The same calm voice.

400
00:11:46,776 --> 00:11:48,020
Reading names.

401
00:11:48,801 --> 00:11:50,363
Rule sixteen.

402
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:52,150
When the radio starts reading names,

403
00:11:52,172 --> 00:11:53,550
turn it off.

404
00:11:53,518 --> 00:11:55,579
At first, they're names you don't know.

405
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:56,609
Then it reads Mrs.

406
00:11:56,481 --> 00:11:57,382
Hale.

407
00:11:57,350 --> 00:11:59,003
Then Mr. Alvarez.

408
00:11:59,087 --> 00:12:01,240
Then it reads your street.

409
00:12:01,209 --> 00:12:02,588
Your house number.

410
00:12:02,674 --> 00:12:04,873
Grandma pulls the plug out of the wall.

411
00:12:04,839 --> 00:12:07,584
The radio keeps talking for three more seconds.

412
00:12:07,553 --> 00:12:09,001
Then it stops in the middle of a

413
00:12:08,919 --> 00:12:09,979
name.

414
00:12:09,947 --> 00:12:11,600
You never find out whose.

415
00:12:12,233 --> 00:12:13,043
In the morning,

416
00:12:13,007 --> 00:12:14,978
the Hales' car is gone.

417
00:12:14,946 --> 00:12:17,464
So is the whole Alvarez family.

418
00:12:18,245 --> 00:12:19,625
Rule seventeen.

419
00:12:19,612 --> 00:12:21,970
Keep one phone that has never heard your

420
00:12:21,876 --> 00:12:23,085
voice.

421
00:12:23,053 --> 00:12:25,195
Grandma opens her closet and takes out a

422
00:12:25,102 --> 00:12:26,117
box.

423
00:12:26,084 --> 00:12:28,431
Inside, there's an old flip phone,

424
00:12:28,486 --> 00:12:30,195
still in its plastic.

425
00:12:30,163 --> 00:12:31,781
She bought it in 1988,

426
00:12:31,711 --> 00:12:32,954
after the first time,

427
00:12:33,123 --> 00:12:34,957
and never turned it on.

428
00:12:34,925 --> 00:12:36,736
It has never heard a single word in

429
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:37,806
this house.

430
00:12:37,775 --> 00:12:39,984
So it's the only phone that can't be

431
00:12:39,891 --> 00:12:41,157
imitated.

432
00:12:41,125 --> 00:12:43,141
You call Mom on it at noon.

433
00:12:43,109 --> 00:12:45,080
She answers on the first ring.

434
00:12:45,048 --> 00:12:46,963
And for the first time all week,

435
00:12:47,018 --> 00:12:48,146
you hear her laugh,

436
00:12:48,372 --> 00:12:50,343
and it's actually her.

437
00:12:50,310 --> 00:12:53,010
Night seven. The last call.

438
00:12:53,399 --> 00:12:54,596
On the seventh night,

439
00:12:54,685 --> 00:12:57,282
every phone on Earth goes silent.

440
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:58,402
No signal.

441
00:12:58,487 --> 00:12:59,821
No internet.

442
00:12:59,906 --> 00:13:01,285
No dial tone.

443
00:13:01,371 --> 00:13:03,979
And somehow, that's worse.

444
00:13:03,947 --> 00:13:06,214
Because silence means it doesn't need the phones

445
00:13:06,110 --> 00:13:07,329
anymore.

446
00:13:07,297 --> 00:13:08,278
Out on the street,

447
00:13:08,299 --> 00:13:10,440
the people who answered are standing on their

448
00:13:10,336 --> 00:13:11,317
lawns.

449
00:13:11,284 --> 00:13:13,711
All of them facing the same direction.

450
00:13:13,678 --> 00:13:15,149
Toward your house.

451
00:13:15,979 --> 00:13:17,359
Rule eighteen.

452
00:13:17,346 --> 00:13:20,319
Write down every number you need on paper.

453
00:13:20,286 --> 00:13:21,120
Mom.

454
00:13:21,205 --> 00:13:22,448
The doctor.

455
00:13:22,532 --> 00:13:23,821
The neighbors.

456
00:13:23,906 --> 00:13:25,831
And write the rules down too.

457
00:13:25,799 --> 00:13:26,951
In pen.

458
00:13:27,036 --> 00:13:28,917
In your own handwriting.

459
00:13:28,884 --> 00:13:30,423
Because on the seventh night,

460
00:13:30,387 --> 00:13:32,631
your phone turns on by itself.

461
00:13:32,599 --> 00:13:34,206
The Notes app is open.

462
00:13:34,174 --> 00:13:35,644
And the rules are there.

463
00:13:35,611 --> 00:13:36,763
All of them.

464
00:13:36,848 --> 00:13:38,820
Only a few words are different.

465
00:13:39,601 --> 00:13:41,208
Rule nineteen.

466
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:43,439
Never read the rules out loud.

467
00:13:43,407 --> 00:13:44,740
That's how it learned them.

468
00:13:44,708 --> 00:13:46,793
Every time someone read them to their family,

469
00:13:46,882 --> 00:13:48,273
it was listening.

470
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:50,849
And now it knows exactly which words to

471
00:13:50,767 --> 00:13:51,805
change.

472
00:13:51,773 --> 00:13:53,152
Grandma knew.

473
00:13:53,237 --> 00:13:55,311
That's why her notebook was always closed when

474
00:13:55,195 --> 00:13:56,437
you walked in.

475
00:13:56,406 --> 00:13:58,183
At 2:59 AM,

476
00:13:58,204 --> 00:14:00,563
you find something in Grandma's nightstand.

477
00:14:00,530 --> 00:14:01,864
A notebook.

478
00:14:01,949 --> 00:14:03,556
The paper is yellow.

479
00:14:03,524 --> 00:14:06,177
The date on the first page is 1987.

480
00:14:06,145 --> 00:14:07,752
It's the same rules.

481
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:09,053
In her handwriting.

482
00:14:09,139 --> 00:14:10,655
It happened before.

483
00:14:10,740 --> 00:14:11,937
Only once.

484
00:14:12,023 --> 00:14:13,766
Only on landlines.

485
00:14:13,851 --> 00:14:15,504
And she survived it.

486
00:14:15,472 --> 00:14:16,669
On the last page,

487
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:18,228
she wrote one more rule,

488
00:14:18,397 --> 00:14:20,220
underlined three times.

489
00:14:21,001 --> 00:14:22,425
The last rule.

490
00:14:22,414 --> 00:14:24,897
Nothing real will ever ask you to keep

491
00:14:24,804 --> 00:14:25,842
listening.

492
00:14:25,809 --> 00:14:27,279
You read it twice.

493
00:14:27,247 --> 00:14:29,127
Then you realize what time it is.

494
00:14:29,095 --> 00:14:30,611
3:00 AM.

495
00:14:31,735 --> 00:14:33,797
So, let's be honest with each other.

496
00:14:33,765 --> 00:14:35,588
You've been listening to a voice reading you

497
00:14:35,495 --> 00:14:37,784
rules for almost fifteen minutes.

498
00:14:37,753 --> 00:14:39,406
A calm voice.

499
00:14:39,490 --> 00:14:41,347
A voice that sounds like it knows what

500
00:14:41,231 --> 00:14:42,372
it's doing.

501
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:44,038
It read you twenty rules.

502
00:14:44,006 --> 00:14:45,158
Out loud.

503
00:14:45,242 --> 00:14:46,940
Every single one.

504
00:14:47,025 --> 00:14:48,234
And the whole time,

505
00:14:48,289 --> 00:14:50,635
something was listening along with you.

506
00:14:51,467 --> 00:14:53,153
You never once asked it for the code

507
00:14:53,026 --> 00:14:53,802
word.

508
00:14:53,770 --> 00:14:56,105
It's 3:00 AM somewhere right now.

509
00:14:56,073 --> 00:14:57,463
If you've made it this far,

510
00:14:57,484 --> 00:14:59,682
you know twenty ways to stay alive.

511
00:14:59,650 --> 00:15:00,893
Check your phone.

512
00:15:00,978 --> 00:15:03,040
If the caller ID shows your own number,

513
00:15:03,062 --> 00:15:04,862
you already know what to do.

514
00:15:04,829 --> 00:15:06,858
And if you've figured out rule twenty-one,

515
00:15:06,946 --> 00:15:08,759
write it in the comments.

516
00:15:08,726 --> 00:15:10,652
Just don't write your code word.
